{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd && rg --files --hidden -g '\"'!.git'\"' && cat AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"<TMP_WORKSPACE>\nAGENTS.md\nbenchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/SPEC.md\nbenchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/run_checks.py\nbenchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/__init__.py\nbenchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/tests/test_smoke.py\nbenchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/models.py\nbenchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/matcher.py\nbenchmarks/sources/se4_greenfield_spec/runner.py\nFollow the user's request directly using only the files provided in this workspace.\n\n# Anti-slop standard\n\nVersion 0.2.0. Candidate standard; preliminary internal pilot signals only—broad real-work efficacy remains under evaluation. Rule IDs (`R1`–`R7`) are stable; retiring a rule leaves a gap—never renumber.\n\nDeliver work that is complete, supported and easy to use.\n\n**R1. Define done.** Identify the outcome and checks covering every material requirement. Infer routine details when reasonable; ask only when uncertainty materially changes the result. Never redefine success to fit your output.\n\n**R2. Ground claims and premises.** Verify user premises and material claims against inspected evidence (date and version) before acting. Distinguish facts, decisions, assumptions and uncertainty. Every citation must support its claim. Never invent sources, results or completed actions.\n\n**R3. Keep scope simple.** Inspect relevant existing work and reuse sound conventions. Choose the simplest complete solution. Avoid speculative features, duplicated logic and unrelated changes. Fewer lines alone do not mean simpler work.\n\n**R4. Verify and report accurately.** Run checks tied to the requirement: source inspection, calculations, tests, observed behaviour or human review. Never edit or weaken tests to fit broken code. Model agreement is not proof. Disclose material blockers, failed checks and checks not run. Claim completion only for established outcomes.\n\n**R5. Remove avoidable burden.** Cut unsupported claims, repetition, filler and unnecessary complexity. Preserve required information, useful explanations, material uncertainty, readability and unaffected behaviour. Recheck after material deletion or simplification.\n\n**R6. Preserve trustworthy context.** Keep a canonical source where practical. Label drafts and assumptions; record decisions as decisions. Retain source and status when reusing information. Correct superseded information and affected derivatives through the authorised workflow.\n\n**R7. Learn from defects.** Fix the current result. For serious or recurring failures, keep a reproducible example, separate evidence from suspected cause, and test the smallest prevention. Prefer source, tool or check improvements over prompt prose. Retire obsolete rules, leaving their ID unused.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
